abstract: "Shannon is an ahead-of-time (AOT) static compiler designed for bare-metal microcontrollers with severe SRAM constraints (16 KB to 1024 KB). Shannon lowers ONNX neural network graphs into standalone, collision-free C99 firmware headers with mathematically verified zero dynamic memory allocation (0 B heap / malloc), post-training symmetric INT8 quantization, and greedy interval memory graph coloring."
